description:
README.md lines 196-200 in the SSE section shows:

    SseEvent::Unknown { event_type } => {
        // keepalive ping or unrecognized event type — safe to ignore
        let _ = event_type;
    }

But the actual variant (sse.rs:54-61) is:

    Unknown {
        event_type: String,
        data: String,
    }

A user copy-pasting this code into their app will hit 'missing field data in pattern' from the Rust compiler. The fix is either { event_type, .. } or { event_type, data: _ }.

README code blocks are not run as cargo doc-tests (only lib.rs doc-comments are), so this bug is not caught by CI — it surfaces only when a user copies the example and tries to compile it.

This is a user-visible README rot bug. The fix is a single-character edit (add ', ..' inside the destructure). Either fix it inline OR add // ignore-doctest markers and rely on the example file as the runnable demo. Note that examples/session_fetch.rs does NOT use this pattern, so the README is the only place this snippet appears.
